# What the mox form, booted as it ships, without a shell and without a
# config, must say on its console (make check-shellfree-mox; test/boot;
# forms/demo/test/console has the format). Mox, given no admin password,
# parks before mox-setup makes or writes anything, and says why. make
# check-mox boots it with its config, and checks it serves.

seen    mox-needs-config  leash: \{"event":"down","service":"mox","why":"config admin-password: FileNotFound"\}
unseen  setup-ran         mox-setup: (made|mox\.conf|admin)
